13:51.580 --> 13:53.040
This will pressure the economy,

13:53.380 --> 13:55.680
and therefore it will probably pressure markets too

13:55.680 --> 13:56.140
a little bit.

13:56.260 --> 13:58.840
So I much prefer to see something like this,

13:58.920 --> 14:00.400
but again, we'll keep open to this too.

14:00.620 --> 14:01.420
As for the stocks,

14:01.560 --> 14:03.300
they really need to start pushing here,

14:03.380 --> 14:04.540
otherwise we're going to have to accept

14:04.540 --> 14:06.660
this is left translated and heading for

14:06.660 --> 14:08.300
the upcoming daily cycle.

14:08.680 --> 14:10.320
And we'll be declining for the rest of it,

14:10.360 --> 14:11.740
which is still quite a way away.

14:11.840 --> 14:14.580
That would get us out to kind of the 24th of September

14:14.580 --> 14:16.740
for a low somewhere in that neighborhood,

14:16.740 --> 14:19.240
which also would be in time with gold's bottom,

14:19.500 --> 14:19.820
wouldn't it?

14:20.060 --> 14:22.160
So maybe we are going to have that kind of bearish September

14:22.160 --> 14:23.420
before we can move higher.

14:23.720 --> 14:24.580
The Nasdaq so far,

14:24.620 --> 14:26.920
it's not looking too bad so long as it can push, okay?

14:26.940 --> 14:28.300
But we're in that kind of neighborhood now

14:28.300 --> 14:29.900
where it does have to start to push.

14:30.080 --> 14:30.880
Same with the Dow.

14:31.040 --> 14:32.280
If this is just a fake breakdown,

14:32.280 --> 14:34.580
then it has to recover pretty much immediately.

14:34.900 --> 14:37.980
Otherwise, we're going to be having to look for cycle lows

14:37.980 --> 14:40.000
around that kind of late September timeframe.

14:40.480 --> 14:42.540
The Russell's being a little bit worse for wear,

14:42.700 --> 14:44.340
slipping into the red here on the trade.

14:44.480 --> 14:45.980
But again, same things apply.

14:46.100 --> 14:47.200
So long as this thing can push,

14:47.220 --> 14:47.840
then we're good.

14:48.100 --> 14:50.760
And any kind of chop or further lower lows here

14:50.760 --> 14:52.200
would put us in jeopardy

14:52.200 --> 14:53.880
if needed to wait for another daily cycle.

14:54.240 --> 14:55.920
And Bitcoin is still boring everyone to death.

14:56.120 --> 14:58.680
There's still a lot of people cheering on

14:58.680 --> 15:00.420
the bottom being in, of course.

15:00.420 --> 15:01.620
We've seen that in the sentiment.

15:01.840 --> 15:03.660
I'm still making all of the same arguments.

15:03.820 --> 15:05.580
So I don't think I need to repeat myself here.

15:05.900 --> 15:08.600
Where I change my stance are closes above here.

15:08.840 --> 15:10.680
But until such time as we get that,

15:10.900 --> 15:12.480
then I stand with a yellow squiggle.

15:12.760 --> 15:15.020
And the more that people kind of clown on me

15:15.020 --> 15:17.000
or call me sidelined or coping or whatever,

15:17.080 --> 15:18.260
the more that makes me think

15:18.260 --> 15:19.640
I might be correct in this call.

15:19.900 --> 15:22.060
ETH as well has clearly set that resistance line.

15:22.280 --> 15:23.760
So if it's going to break, fine.

15:23.920 --> 15:26.780
Then you've pretty much got a nice tight risk management

15:26.780 --> 15:28.960
around that ball flag break if you want to take it.

15:28.960 --> 15:31.380
But I don't really think it's super likely

15:31.380 --> 15:32.660
at this moment in time.

15:32.900 --> 15:35.360
We have got to tell that to the bond market situation here

15:35.360 --> 15:37.320
because yields keep pushing higher, don't they?

15:37.460 --> 15:40.040
So it's almost like they are going to do the hiking

15:40.040 --> 15:41.500
for the Fed here, isn't it?

15:41.520 --> 15:42.980
It's almost like that's what they want.

15:43.100 --> 15:44.420
Maybe this is just going to be a deviation

15:44.420 --> 15:45.920
and then it finally collapses.

15:46.320 --> 15:47.920
And again, we got clear invalidation, right?

15:47.940 --> 15:50.840
I give up on being bearish yields and bullish bonds

15:50.840 --> 15:52.760
if we can break out the top of this.

15:52.840 --> 15:55.520
But so far, we're just still seemingly about to top

15:55.520 --> 15:56.420
for the weekly cycle.

15:56.560 --> 15:57.700
That's what it looks like to me.

15:57.700 --> 15:59.640
So I think it's fair to say most of these things

15:59.640 --> 16:00.900
are directionally moving

16:00.900 --> 16:03.260
as per the expectations and yellow squiggles.

16:03.600 --> 16:05.820
Yes, we need to exercise some patience in some places.

16:06.320 --> 16:08.200
And yes, we need to keep open to multiple scenarios

16:08.200 --> 16:09.800
